                    "message": "would be interesting to know in which platform you observed the issue and if it is startup related or if it can occur at any  point in time."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "I encountered this on Yv5, where it appears to be startup related. The first attempt to get the CPLD version fails, but the retry succeeds."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/cpld.cpp",
                    "line": 78,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "So we hold the mux here for up to 200ms while we wait to retry. Probably not an issue, just wanted to mention it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "cpld/cpld.cpp",
                    "line": 78,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "In the case I encountered, there is no mux GPIO, so this hold time is skipped."
                }
